# Build context for the image built from the REPO ROOT: apps/web/Dockerfile
# (the contestant app). The poller is built from ./sync with its own
# .dockerignore — it is configured from the environment at runtime, not from
# a build input, so it needs nothing from the root.
#
# Without this the context was 1.3 GB across 54,792 files, and Fly's builder
# reported it on every deploy:
#
#   WARN Build context is 1.3 GB across 54,792 files.
#          apps/    1.2 GB
#          .git/    17 MB
#
# Almost all of that is apps/web/node_modules and .next — neither of which
# belongs in a context, because apps/web/Dockerfile runs `pnpm install
# --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm build` itself. Copying a host-built
# node_modules in would also risk shipping host-architecture native binaries
# into a linux image.
#
# `scorer/` and `sync/` keep their own .dockerignore for the builds that use
# those directories as the context; this file governs the root ones.

# Dependencies — every image installs its own.
**/node_modules

# Build output — every image builds its own.
apps/web/.next
apps/web/out

# History. 17 MB of it, and no image reads it.
.git
.gitignore

# SECRETS. Nothing should COPY these, and keeping them out of the context
# means a careless `COPY . .` in some future Dockerfile cannot pick them up.
# `.env.example` is the committed template and harmless, but nothing needs it
# in an image either.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Local scratch and test artefacts.
state/
docs/superpowers/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Editor/tooling noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
